  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/6f35161e7efbd53c9ef558ffe88d8e046771128965a9fdd02143ae37a9b130ea.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,2-|x|\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/769a521cd6b05ecf05052da382e40295b26be66fe56e4eff7c6940c9032f2f0b.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true.",
